    "note": [
     {
      "text": "36-year-old female presenting with headache with dizziness for 2 days. Character: throbbing at the back of the head; radiation: it does not spread; aggravated by morning time; relieved by rest. Severity 6/10. Associated: blurred vision, palpitations. PMH: Type 2 diabetes for 14 years; Hypertension for 8 years; Hypothyroidism for 7 years. Drugs: Metformin 500 mg; Amlodipine 5 mg; Levothyroxine 50 mcg. Allergy: penicillin. Family: no similar illness. Personal: non-smoker, no alcohol. Triage: ROUTINE."
